  "body": "What happens: the Sinumerik 840D post writes no language-mode word (`G290` Siemens mode, `G291` ISO dialect). The preamble and the cycles mix words of the two modes: Siemens-mode words (`G505`, `G41 NORM`, `ROT`, `CYCLE832`, `MEAS`) next to ISO-dialect drilling cycles (`G73`-`G89`, `G80`). A comment at lines 812-814 says the post \"assumes ISO dialect mode\".\n\nExpected: the program states one mode in its own block, and each word is valid in that mode (for example `G291` with the ISO cycles, or Siemens mode with `CYCLE81`-`CYCLE89`).\n\nEvidence: `assets/posts/sinumerik.cps:501`, `:755-762`, `:812-814` on upstream/main `f0bdc5109`.\n\nA wrong mode gives an alarm; it does not cut a wrong path. The maintainer tested G83 P on a real 840D in ISO mode (#2349). Research: which words that 840D accepts in each mode, before code.\n\nFound by the post audit against the SINUMERIK manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means: a recorded decision on the mode, and the post writes only words of that mode.\n",
